# MC-E1-F1. L §6.1: "A model is one or more .tally files in one directory tree"; "A member's asks are asked by name in
# a run of the joint model, as a.q, and answered by the member alone"; "each member stays reproducible alone". L §6.4:
# an ask that names a scenario loads with that scenario's file, and L §5.18 checks a line only in the worlds it is
# evaluated in. The member's base ask q pins its own scenario s1 (in its tree): the joint model loads (jq), and m.q is
# answered by the member alone, s1 loaded (world: s1). snap9 refused every joint model over the member (member m:
# LOAD-SCENARIO ask q names s1, neither the model nor a loaded scenario).
=== j/joint.tally
model j
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use m = "../m" sha256 "fd36f989d72da462c1799e54895808d975e256f427a999abe300da4dd81165cb"

ask jq: m.x law 2026-06-30
=== m/model.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

input x: int question "x?"

ask q: x with scenario s1 law 2026-06-30
=== m/scenarios/s1.tally
scenario s1 over m
  tally 2
  from 2026-03-01
=== expect jq m.q
jq: ?"x?" (m.x)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
m.q: ?"x?" (x)
  world: s1
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
